# RC1 exact-source integration patch/spec: PlatformImage + RG35XXImageCache
# Upstream owner remains org.recompile.mobile.PlatformImage.
# Do NOT create a replacement PlatformImage or a second image cache.
# Task: RGJ-RC1-006

Target: src/org/recompile/mobile/PlatformImage.java (TASEmulators/freej2me-plus devel)
Helper: src/org/recompile/mobile/RG35XXImageCache.java

## Byte-array constructor integration

In PlatformImage(byte[] imageData, int imageOffset, int imageLength, boolean mutable):

1. Only immutable images (`mutable == false`) are cache eligible.
2. Compute key with RG35XXImageCache.keyForBytes(imageData, imageOffset, imageLength).
3. On cache hit, construct a fresh TYPE_INT_ARGB BufferedImage, obtain its DataBufferInt array,
   and copy cached ARGB pixels into that fresh backing array. Never expose/share the cached array.
4. On cache miss, preserve the existing ImageIO decode and type-normalization path exactly.
5. After decode/normalization and after any RG35XX PNG/tRNS compatibility repair in the consolidated
   PlatformImage path, put the final ARGB pixels into RG35XXImageCache only when immutable.
6. Preserve `isMutable = mutable` exactly.

Pseudo-diff (adapt to exact consolidated source; do not apply blindly):

@@ PlatformImage(byte[] imageData, int imageOffset, int imageLength, boolean mutable)
+ String rgCacheKey = null;
+ if(!mutable) {
+     rgCacheKey = RG35XXImageCache.keyForBytes(imageData, imageOffset, imageLength);
+     int[] rgCached = RG35XXImageCache.get(rgCacheKey);
+     if(rgCached != null) {
+         // Width/height must be part of cached metadata before this fast return can be used.
+         // Current RG35XXImageCache stores pixels only, therefore DO NOT implement an unsafe
+         // cache-hit return yet. See RC1 audit decision below.
+     }
+ }
  // existing ImageIO decode/type normalization remains authoritative
  ...
+ if(!mutable && rgCacheKey != null) RG35XXImageCache.put(rgCacheKey, dataBuffer);
  isMutable = mutable;

## RC1 audit decision: cache metadata gap

The current RG35XXImageCache stores only int[] pixels, not decoded width/height. Therefore an exact
PlatformImage cache-hit reconstruction cannot be implemented safely without either:
(a) extending the existing RG35XXImageCache Entry/API to retain dimensions, or
(b) decoding image headers again, which defeats the intended decode-cache fast path.

RC1 chooses (a), but that modification must be made as a MODIFY of the existing registered class,
not by adding a new cache class/package. Until the dimension-aware API is committed and audited,
this patch is an integration specification and MUST NOT be marked BUILD-PASS.

## Mutable/immutable invariants

- PlatformImage(int Width, int Height) and color-backed blank images remain mutable and are never cached.
- PlatformImage(Image source) remains a deep copy via System.arraycopy; no cache sharing.
- PlatformImage(com.nttdocomo.ui.Image source) remains a deep copy; DoJa mutability semantics are preserved.
- DoJa byte-array constructor calls with mutable=true bypass cache completely.
- getMIDPGraphics()/getDoJaGraphics() immutable checks remain unchanged.
- Resource-name/InputStream constructors remain uncached in RC1 unless a later task defines a stable identity key.
- PNG indexed transparency/tRNS repair, when present in the RG35XX consolidated source, must execute before cache insertion.

## Duplicate-prevention result

No new RG35XX Java class/package is required for this gate. Existing owner pair is authoritative:
PlatformImage (upstream facade/decoder) + RG35XXImageCache (target immutable cache).
